# The repositories alma10's packages come from, in order of preference. An
# unlocked build installs from these; scripts/rpm-lock.py lock resolves the
# packages that build installed against them, into alma10.lock.
# Fedora's EPEL 10 is built for x86-64-v3 and won't run on x86-64-v2 hosts,
# so epel is AlmaLinux's x86_64_v2 rebuild; epel-release from extras points
# the installed system at it. These are the URLs of AlmaLinux's own stable
# x86_64_v2 kickstarts (github.com/AlmaLinux/sig-livemedia).
baseos    https://repo.almalinux.org/almalinux/10/BaseOS/x86_64_v2/os/
appstream https://repo.almalinux.org/almalinux/10/AppStream/x86_64_v2/os/
crb       https://repo.almalinux.org/almalinux/10/CRB/x86_64_v2/os/
extras    https://repo.almalinux.org/almalinux/10/extras/x86_64_v2/os/
epel      https://repo.almalinux.org/almalinux-epel/10z/x86_64_v2/
